 or kitchen","units":"percent of homes","direction":"down","source":"IPUMS Census/ACS (from EB)","note":"In 1960, 1 in 7 homes lacked complete plumbing. Today it is essentially gone.","asof":"2023","series":[{"name":"Lacking complete plumbing","data":[[1960,14.71],[1970,5.52],[1980,1.46],[1990,0.78],[2000,0.64],[2005,0.44],[2010,0.57],[2015,0.43],[2019,0.38],[2023,0.42]]},{"name":"Lacking complete kitchen","data":[[1960,1.22],[1970,3.06],[1980,1.87],[1990,0.72],[2000,0.68],[2005,0.58],[2010,0.96],[2015,0.82],[2019,0.84],[2023,0.82]]}]},{"id":"crowding","title":"Overcrowding","units":"percent of homes (>1 person per room)","direction":"down","source":"IPUMS Census/ACS (from EB)","note":"Overcrowding fell from ~11% in 1960 to ~3.5%.","asof":"2023","series":[{"name":"Overcrowded homes","data":[[1960,11.45],[1970,7.98],[1980,4.26],[1990,4.69],[2000,5.75],[2005,3.09],[2010,3.37],[2015,3.44],[2019,3.32],[2023,3.52]]}]},{"id":"space","title":"Space per person","units":"count per person","direction":"up","source":"IPUMS Census/ACS (from EB)","note":"Bedrooms and rooms per person have risen steadily \u2014 more room even as families shrank.","asof":"2023","series":[{"name":"Bedrooms per person","data":[[1960,0.703],[1970,0.789],[1980,0.913],[1990,0.976],[2000,1.002],[2005,1.077],[2010,1.096],[2015,1.101],[2019,1.117],[2023,1.126]]},{"name":"Rooms per person","data":[[1960,1.507],[1970,1.646],[1980,1.938],[1990,2.047],[2000,2.105],[2005,2.216],[2010,2.33],[2015,2.355],[2019,2.384],[2023,2.401]]}]},{"id":"spare-bedroom","title":"Families with a spare bedroom","units":"percent of families","direction":"up","source":"IPUMS Census/ACS (from EB)","note":"A majority of families now have more bedrooms than they strictly need.","asof":"2023","series":[{"name":"Families with a spare bedroom","data":[[1960,48.23],[1970,55.87],[1980,69.41],[1990,70.06],[2000,70.14],[2005,75.34],[2010,75.95],[2015,75.75],[2019,76.36],[2023,77.88]]}]},{"id":"new-home-size","title":"Size of a new single-fa